# Build context for server/Dockerfile is server/. Keep the context tight and
# keep every secret out of it: in November 2026 a baked .env in a public
# Docker image leaked production credentials. The Dockerfile also uses narrow
# COPY instructions; this file is the backstop, not the only defense.

# Dependencies and build output are rebuilt inside the image.
node_modules
dist

# Secrets and local configuration: never in the build context, never in a layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Logs and test artifacts.
*.log
npm-debug.log*
coverage
test-results

# VCS metadata.
.git
